# Preserve the original missions, mission order, world layout, progression, gameplay…

Preserve the original missions, mission order, world layout, progression,
gameplay structure, models, textures, audio, cinematics, UI, and localization.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Preserve the original missions, mission order, world layout, progression,
  gameplay structure, models, textures, audio, cinematics, UI, and
  localization, with English in the canonical base and other supported official
  languages preserved through deterministic language mods.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

Normalized mission-script intake is source-backed and fail-closed. JSON decoding
now lives in pipeline composition, while the mission domain owns only typed
normalized evidence plus structural and semantic validation. The crate-level
intake rejects unknown or malformed wire fields before domain validation, and
817 pipeline library tests cover the resulting mission graph, objective,
condition, reference, ordering, and Unreal-preparation behavior without private
game data in test fixtures.

Canonical non-English localization remains outside the English base and
publishes
through deterministic normalized language-mod packages. Current language tests
cover source read-only containment, official track mapping, missing-evidence
failure, deterministic repeated output, package publication, and manifest/report
agreement without synthesizing unavailable Italian content.

This parent remains open because complete progression/gameplay verification and
final cross-platform release evidence are broader than these preserved mission
and localization boundaries.
